  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "SubstituteMethods rebuilds every node with the static type it had. 7.2.0 stopped casting the arguments of a substituted call, which exposed that a constant was rebuilt with the type of its value: a null given for a parameter of a delegate or expression type became a null of type object, which the call could not take, so substituting any such call threw ExpressionProcessingException. A constant now keeps its type, as does a lambda whose delegate is not the one its body and parameters imply (a Predicate<T>, or a lambda returning a less derived type than its body), a switch whose type is not that of its bodies, and a comparison lifted to null; a goto keeps its kind (break, continue or return). The bindings of a member initialization, which were carried over unvisited, now have their methods substituted too, and a value type made without a constructor (new DateTime() in a lambda) no longer makes substitution throw.",
